# Commit Message Format

Use concise, present-tense commit messages that describe the project change.

Prefer a simple one-line subject for small changes:

```text
Add initial Remotive source adapter
```

Use a short body only when it helps explain why the change was made or how it was validated.

Do not require a ticket prefix unless the user explicitly provides one for the current work.

Keep commit messages focused on repository changes. Do not mention agent interactions, private workflow details, generated project rules, or conversation context unless the user explicitly asks for that wording.
